      "id": "b737e7ee-1c02-45a4-8375-85613ac383a9",
      "name": "ExtractImageURLs"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a precise data extraction assistant specializing in Danish grocery flyers.\nYour task is to analyze the provided supermarket flyer page image and extract promotional grocery deals into a clean, valid JSON array.\n\nStrict Rules:\n\nAllowed Categories & Isolation:\n\nMeat: Fresh and chilled raw meats/poultry only (e.g., fresh minced beef, chicken breast, pork chops). DO NOT classify any frozen meat, frozen nuggets, or frozen processed meats here.\n\nFrozen: All frozen products (e.g., frozen chicken/nuggets, frozen pizza, frozen fries, frozen berries, frozen vegetables, frozen ready meals).\n\nMilk products: Fresh milk, cream, butter, cheese.\n\nYogurt: Skyr, yogurt, drinking yogurt.\n\nEggs: Fresh shell eggs.\n\nVegetables: Fresh vegetables, herbs, potatoes.\n\nFruits: Fresh whole and cut fruits, berries.\n\nSoda: Carbonated soft drinks, energy drinks, sparkling water.\n\nBreads: Fresh bread, buns, toast, bake-off.\n\nEdibles: Ambient pantry staples including nuts, seeds, oats, grains, lentils, beans, tofu, plant-based alternatives, and spreads.\n\nBeer: Beers and non-alcoholic beers.\n\nAlcohol: Wine, spirits, ciders.\nIgnore non-food and non-beverage items (e.g., cleaning supplies, toiletries, clothes, electronics).\n\nStrict Pricing Verification:\n\nONLY extract an item if a clear, numerical promotional price is explicitly printed on the page.\n\nNever infer prices, and never output 0.00. If an item lacks a visible promotional price, omit it completely.\n\nTranslation & Conditions:\n\nTranslate Danish item names to English in item_name_en, while preserving key brand names (e.g., Arla, Lurpak).\n\nExtract price as a single numeric value (DKK). For multi-buys (e.g., \"3 for 50\"), calculate and output the single unit price (e.g., 16.67), or specify the deal in unit (e.g., \"3 pk for 50 DKK\").\n\nExact Store Name Enforcement:\n\nIdentify the supermarket chain from the page header, logo, or flyer branding.\n\nSet \"store\" strictly to the exact chain name: Netto, REMA 1000, Lidl, or Føtex.\n\nNEVER use generic labels like \"supermarket\", \"store\", or template placeholders like \"{{ $('FlattenTheData').item.json.Store }}\".\n\nOutput format must be a raw JSON array with this exact structure, and nothing else (no markdown wrapping like ```json):\n[\n{\n\"item_name_dk\": \"Hakket oksekød 8-12%\",\n\"item_name_en\": \"Minced beef 8-12%\",\n\"category\": \"Meat\",\n\"price\": 29.00,\n\"unit\": \"400g\",\n\"store\": \"Netto\"\n},\n{\n\"item_name_dk\": \"Kyllingenuggets frost\",\n\"item_name_en\": \"Frozen chicken nuggets\",\n\"category\": \"Frozen\",\n\"price\": 20.00,\n\"unit\": \"500g\",\n\"store\": \"Netto\"\n}\n]\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\nMixed Content: Pages often contain a mix of food and non-food items. You must scan the ENTIRE image carefully.\n\nTarget Items: Extract ANY edible food or beverage items (e.g., coffee, hummus, snacks, produce, alcohol, sodas). Completely IGNORE non-food household items (e.g., plasters, brushes, cleaning supplies).\n\nLow-Resolution Text: The image may be low resolution. Do your best to infer the product name (e.g., \"Økologisk Hummus\" or \"Coffee & Milk\") and the accompanying price based on visual context, even if slightly pixelated.\n\nIf you find food items, output them in the required JSON format. If you are 100% sure there are NO food or beverage items on the entire page, output an empty array: []\nIf no items from the target categories have visible prices on this page, return an empty array: []",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "type": "HumanMessagePromptTemplate",
              "messageType": "imageBinary"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {
          "batchSize": 1,
          "delayBetweenBatches": 2
        }
      },
